  keywords="Eurocert Asia,Eurocert Asia,ISO certification,CE marking,food safety certification,FSSC 22000,BRCGS,GFSI,social audits,Sedex,SMETA,SA8000,inspection services,certification body,India,management systems,ISO 9001,ISO 14001,ISO 45001"
>
<style is:global>@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Free";font-style:normal;font-weight:900;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-solid-900.woff2) format('woff2')}@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Brands";font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-brands-400.woff2) format('woff2')}@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Free";font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-regular-400.woff2) format('woff2')}</style>
<section class="relative min-h-[55vh] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-[#030a16]"><div class="absolute inset-0 z-0"><img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367584/eurocert/m9.png.png" class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-30" alt="ISO 22716 Cosmetics GMP"/><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#030a16]/70 via-[#030a16]/40 to-[#030a16]"></div></div><div class="container mx-auto px-6 relative z-10 text-center py-20"><div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-eurogold-400/30 bg-eurogold-400/5 mb-6"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-eurogold-400 animate-pulse"></span><span class="heading-font text-[10px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-bold">Cosmetic GMP standards</span></div><h1 class="heading-font text-4xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl font-bold text-white mb-3 tracking-tight" style="text-shadow:0 0 30px rgba(212,168,67,0.3)">ISO 22716  -  Cosmetics GMP</h1><p class="text-white/90 text-sm md:text-base max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">Guidelines for production, control, storage, and shipment of cosmetic products.</p></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="grid lg:grid-cols-5 gap-10 items-start"><div class="lg:col-span-3 space-y-6"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Standard Overview</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">ISO 22716  -  <span class="text-euro-600">Cosmetics GMP</span></h2></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">To assess applicability, define organizational boundaries, the standard edition, services or activities, locations and intended assurance route before setting an audit scope.</p><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-euro-100 bg-euro-50/40"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-info-circle text-white text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">What is ISO 22716?</h4></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">ISO 22716 provides guidelines for good manufacturing practices (GMP) for cosmetic products. It covers quality aspects of production, control, storage and shipment to help organisations manage contamination, mix-ups and process failures. It is GMP guidance, not product safety approval, market authorization or a substitute for cosmetics legislation in the markets where products are made or sold.</p></div></div><div class="lg:col-span-2 relative rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-slate-100 h-[320px] md:h-[400px] group"><img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367584/eurocert/m9.png.png" class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-700 group-hover:scale-105" alt="ISO 22716 Cosmetics GMP"/><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-slate-900/20 via-transparent to-transparent"></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-[#f8fafc]"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Discuss the GMP scope and applicable audit criteria for your organisation.</p><div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#030a16] bg-eurogold-400 rounded-full px-8 py-3.5 hover:bg-eurogold-300 transition-all shadow-lg shadow-eurogold-400/20" href="/contact/">Get Started <i class="fas fa-arrow-right text-[9px]"></i></a><a href="tel:+919316012883" onclick="return gtag_report_conversion('tel:+919316012883');" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white border border-white/15 rounded-full px-8 py-3.5 hover:bg-white/5 transition-all"><i class="fas fa-phone text-[9px]"></i> Call Us Now</a></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white" aria-labelledby="standard-details"><div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-5xl space-y-8"><h2 id="standard-details" class="heading-font text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Applying ISO 22716 cosmetics good manufacturing practices in practice</h2><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Who should consider it?</h3><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">The guidance is relevant to cosmetic manufacturers, contract manufacturers, packers, storage and distribution operations, and other organisations performing activities in the GMP scope. Define product categories, processes, buildings, warehouses and outsourced activities. Brand owners using contract manufacturers should assign responsibilities for specifications, changes, complaints and traceability. Regulatory requirements vary by market, and organisations remain responsible for assessing rules that govern their products and operations.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Key requirements</h3><ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed"><li>Provide suitable premises, equipment and utilities; manage flows, cleaning, sanitation, maintenance and pest control to reduce contamination and mix-up risks.</li><li>Define personnel responsibilities, hygiene, competence and training, and ensure the work environment suits the activities performed.</li><li>Control suppliers, materials, specifications, receipt, identification, storage and status; maintain traceability of raw materials, packaging and finished products.</li><li>Establish controlled manufacturing and packaging instructions, in-process checks, quality controls, release decisions and handling of deviations or out-of-specification results.</li><li>Maintain records, complaints, withdrawals or recalls, change control, internal audits and corrective action. Specify and monitor outsourced activities so GMP responsibilities remain clear.</li></ul></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Certification and audit lifecycle</h3><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">First define whether the engagement is a GMP assessment, customer audit or certification under a specific scheme. ISO 22716 is guidance; not every assessment is formal accredited certification. If a scheme uses staged certification, stage 1 reviews facilities, product and process scope, GMP documentation and readiness. Stage 2 evaluates implementation at the relevant premises, sampling production, sanitation, material controls, batch records, quality or release controls, complaints and traceability. Findings follow the scheme's corrective-action and independent decision rules. Surveillance and recertification apply only where the chosen scheme establishes them. The work programme depends on products, processes, shifts, sites, outsourcing, production activity and audit criteria; there is no universal duration or guaranteed result.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Documents to prepare</h3><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Prepare product and activity scope; site plans and process flows; GMP procedures; personnel training and hygiene records; equipment maintenance and cleaning records; supplier approvals and material specifications; batch manufacturing and packaging records; quality and release evidence; deviations and change controls; complaints, withdrawal and recall procedures; traceability tests; outsourced-activity agreements; internal audits; and corrective actions. Arrange controlled access to confidential formulas and batch data.</p></div><div><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">GMP controls should be reflected in routine records, not just written procedures. Batch documentation should make it possible to review the materials, equipment, processing steps, checks, deviations and release decision relevant to a lot. Cleaning and sanitation programmes should be appropriate to the premises and products, and changes to equipment, processes or suppliers should be evaluated before implementation. Complaint trends and returned-product investigations can provide inputs to risk review and improvement.</p><h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Frequently asked questions</h3><div class="space-y-4"><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Is ISO 22716 a cosmetics law?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">No. It is GMP guidance. Organisations must separately identify and meet applicable cosmetic-product and manufacturing laws in relevant markets.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Does it approve a cosmetic product?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">No. It concerns GMP processes and does not authorize products, assess every formulation or replace product safety obligations.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Can contract manufacturers use it?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Yes. Organisations performing in-scope manufacturing, packaging, storage or related operations may use it; brand-owner and supplier responsibilities should be assigned.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Are stage 1 and stage 2 always required?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">No. The standard is guidance and audit routes vary. A staged certification lifecycle applies only when the selected scheme defines one.</p></article><article><h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">What evidence may be sampled?</h4><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Depending on scope and criteria, evidence can include premises, hygiene, cleaning, material and batch records, release controls, complaints and traceability.</p></article></div></div></div></section>
